# Preview email means preview only

When the user says **preview email**, **preview emails**, **run a preview**, or **send me a preview**:

Send a review copy to the named inbox (default `pat@road2media.com`) through a **local Resend preview script**. That send does not go through production delivery.

Use one of:

- `scripts/send-local-email-preview.mjs`
- `scripts/canary-tour-rankings-preview.mjs`
- `scripts/canary-show-recap-narrative-preview.mjs`

## Never on that request

A single admin address does not make a live send a preview. Do not:

- Call `runCommsTrigger` with `dryRun: false`, including `scripts/canary-comms-preview.mjs`
- Run a replay or scheduler with `--confirm` (for example `scripts/replay-tour-rankings-daily.mjs --confirm`)
- Fan out a real payload, even to one uid
- Write `fcm_notification_log`, `commsInbox`, or the daily email cap

A dry run that sends nothing is not a preview email. Wait for an explicit live-send instruction (`send it`, `send the live recap`, `--confirm`) before any production delivery.
